3. Background

Describe the current application.

Example:

The backend routine is packaged as a JAR and executed within the existing enterprise application/runtime framework. The routine uses Spring-based configuration and ResourceBundleMessageSource to read configuration parameters from external properties files.

Certain external-system credentials such as usernames and passwords are currently maintained in plaintext in the properties file.

These properties are subsequently accessed by Java code through Spring’s ResourceBundleMessageSource.

As per the security guidelines, sensitive credentials must not be maintained in plaintext. The encryption key must also be maintained separately from the encrypted credentials and must be accessible only to the authorized application/service account.

