5. Problem Statement

Suggested detailed wording

Sensitive credentials are currently stored in plaintext in the external properties configuration file consumed by the backend routine.

This implementation creates a security risk because users/processes having access to the configuration file may be able to obtain the credentials without requiring access to the application runtime.

The current implementation also does not provide adequate separation between the encrypted data and the cryptographic key.

The proposed change will introduce encrypted credential storage and secure key management while preserving the existing properties-based configuration mechanism and minimizing changes to existing routine/business logic.

