9. Encryption Algorithm

Document this carefully.

Recommended:

Algorithm       : AES
Key size        : 256 bits
Mode            : GCM
Padding         : NoPadding
Authentication  : GCM authentication tag
IV/Nonce        : 12 bytes
Tag size        : 128 bits
Encoding        : Base64

Therefore:

AES-256-GCM

Why GCM?

AES-GCM provides both confidentiality and integrity/authentication of the encrypted data. A unique IV/nonce will be generated for each encryption operation.

Avoid specifying:

AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding

in the TS.

Also don’t design your own encryption format.

⸻

10. Encryption Data Format

Define the format clearly.

For example:

ENC(v1:<Base64-IV>:<Base64-Ciphertext>)

Example:

ENC(v1:AbCdEf123...:XyZaBc456...)

Explain:

Component	Description
ENC	Indicates encrypted configuration value
v1	Encryption format/key version
IV	AES-GCM initialization vector
Ciphertext	Encrypted credential
Base64	Text-safe encoding for properties file

This is useful for future key rotation.

