34. Memory Considerations

A subtle but good technical point.

Once decrypted:

ENC(...)
   ↓
String plaintext

the plaintext exists in JVM memory.

Therefore:

The solution protects credentials at rest. It does not eliminate the existence of plaintext credentials during runtime. The decrypted credential should be retained in memory only for the minimum required duration and must never be logged or persisted.

This demonstrates good security understanding.

